[{"id":2346680624,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIzNDY2ODA2MjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/2346680624","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2019-05-16T14:38:48Z","label":{"name":"bug","color":"d73a4a"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":2346680628,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIzNDY2ODA2Mjg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/2346680628","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2019-05-16T14:38:49Z","label":{"name":"orm","color":"20C0B0"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/493098242","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4686#issuecomment-493098242","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4686","id":493098242,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5MzA5ODI0Mg==","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-05-16T14:45:40Z","updated_at":"2019-05-16T14:45:40Z","body":"the relationship .entity level mutex does not seem to fix the issue, since above I've purposely made the \"delay\" occur in declarative before the actual mapping starts up:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/relationships.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/relationships.py\r\nindex b40fad332b..e70d4ed42c 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/relationships.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/relationships.py\r\n@@ -1821,29 +1821,33 @@ class RelationshipProperty(StrategizedProperty):\r\n         class or aliased class tha is referred towards.\r\n \r\n         \"\"\"\r\n-        if util.callable(self.argument) and not isinstance(\r\n-            self.argument, (type, mapperlib.Mapper)\r\n-        ):\r\n-            argument = self.argument()\r\n-        else:\r\n-            argument = self.argument\r\n+        mapperlib._CONFIGURE_MUTEX.acquire()\r\n+        try:\r\n+            if util.callable(self.argument) and not isinstance(\r\n+                self.argument, (type, mapperlib.Mapper)\r\n+            ):\r\n+                argument = self.argument()\r\n+            else:\r\n+                argument = self.argument\r\n \r\n-        if isinstance(argument, type):\r\n-            return mapperlib.class_mapper(argument, configure=False)\r\n+            if isinstance(argument, type):\r\n+                return mapperlib.class_mapper(argument, configure=False)\r\n \r\n-        try:\r\n-            entity = inspect(argument)\r\n-        except sa_exc.NoInspectionAvailable:\r\n-            pass\r\n-        else:\r\n-            if hasattr(entity, \"mapper\"):\r\n-                return entity\r\n+            try:\r\n+                entity = inspect(argument)\r\n+            except sa_exc.NoInspectionAvailable:\r\n+                pass\r\n+            else:\r\n+                if hasattr(entity, \"mapper\"):\r\n+                    return entity\r\n \r\n-        raise sa_exc.ArgumentError(\r\n-            \"relationship '%s' expects \"\r\n-            \"a class or a mapper argument (received: %s)\"\r\n-            % (self.key, type(argument))\r\n-        )\r\n+            raise sa_exc.ArgumentError(\r\n+                \"relationship '%s' expects \"\r\n+                \"a class or a mapper argument (received: %s)\"\r\n+                % (self.key, type(argument))\r\n+            )\r\n+        finally:\r\n+            mapperlib._CONFIGURE_MUTEX.release()\r\n \r\n     @util.memoized_property\r\n     def mapper(self):\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nif OTOH we mutex in the whole declarative metaclass, then the above race does not occur:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/ext/declarative/base.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/ext/declarative/base.py\r\nindex 62db282d1f..76e253293c 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/ext/declarative/base.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/ext/declarative/base.py\r\n@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ from ... import util\r\n from ...orm import class_mapper\r\n from ...orm import exc as orm_exc\r\n from ...orm import mapper\r\n+from ...orm import mapperlib\r\n from ...orm import synonym\r\n from ...orm.attributes import QueryableAttribute\r\n from ...orm.base import _is_mapped_class\r\n@@ -155,7 +156,12 @@ class _MapperConfig(object):\r\n             cfg_cls = _DeferredMapperConfig\r\n         else:\r\n             cfg_cls = _MapperConfig\r\n-        cfg_cls(cls_, classname, dict_)\r\n+\r\n+        mapperlib._CONFIGURE_MUTEX.acquire()\r\n+        try:\r\n+            cfg_cls(cls_, classname, dict_)\r\n+        finally:\r\n+            mapperlib._CONFIGURE_MUTEX.release()\r\n \r\n     def __init__(self, cls_, classname, dict_):\r\n \r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/493098242/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":2346722482,"node_id":"MDE1Ok1pbGVzdG9uZWRFdmVudDIzNDY3MjI0ODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/2346722482","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"milestoned","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2019-05-16T14:50:57Z","milestone":{"title":"1.3.xx"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/493103017","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4686#issuecomment-493103017","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4686","id":493103017,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5MzEwMzAxNw==","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-05-16T14:57:18Z","updated_at":"2019-05-16T14:57:18Z","body":"OK so the best mutex we can do here, is that the class is in the registry; we expect that when it is pulled from the registry, it is compatible with configure_mappers():\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/ext/declarative/base.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/ext/declarative/base.py\r\nindex 62db282d1f..622a837363 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/ext/declarative/base.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/ext/declarative/base.py\r\n@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ from ... import util\r\n from ...orm import class_mapper\r\n from ...orm import exc as orm_exc\r\n from ...orm import mapper\r\n+from ...orm import mapperlib\r\n from ...orm import synonym\r\n from ...orm.attributes import QueryableAttribute\r\n from ...orm.base import _is_mapped_class\r\n@@ -155,6 +156,7 @@ class _MapperConfig(object):\r\n             cfg_cls = _DeferredMapperConfig\r\n         else:\r\n             cfg_cls = _MapperConfig\r\n+\r\n         cfg_cls(cls_, classname, dict_)\r\n \r\n     def __init__(self, cls_, classname, dict_):\r\n@@ -177,17 +179,21 @@ class _MapperConfig(object):\r\n \r\n         self._scan_attributes()\r\n \r\n-        clsregistry.add_class(self.classname, self.cls)\r\n+        mapperlib._CONFIGURE_MUTEX.acquire()\r\n+        try:\r\n+            clsregistry.add_class(self.classname, self.cls)\r\n \r\n-        self._extract_mappable_attributes()\r\n+            self._extract_mappable_attributes()\r\n \r\n-        self._extract_declared_columns()\r\n+            self._extract_declared_columns()\r\n \r\n-        self._setup_table()\r\n+            self._setup_table()\r\n \r\n-        self._setup_inheritance()\r\n+            self._setup_inheritance()\r\n \r\n-        self._early_mapping()\r\n+            self._early_mapping()\r\n+        finally:\r\n+            mapperlib._CONFIGURE_MUTEX.release()\r\n \r\n     def _early_mapping(self):\r\n         self.map()\r\n\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/493103017/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/493103891","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4686#issuecomment-493103891","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4686","id":493103891,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5MzEwMzg5MQ==","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-05-16T14:59:20Z","updated_at":"2019-05-16T14:59:20Z","body":"however, if I make the test script like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndef make_b(Base):\r\n    global B\r\n\r\n    time.sleep(random.random() / 100)\r\n    class B(Base):\r\n        __tablename__ = \"b\"\r\n        id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n\r\n        @declared_attr\r\n        def data(cls):\r\n            time.sleep(.001)\r\n            return Column(String)\r\n\r\n        a_id = Column(ForeignKey(\"a.id\"))\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nthat is, delay before the class even gets put into the registry, which is outside of SQLAlchemy's control, they still get a race:\r\n\r\n`sqlalchemy.exc.InvalidRequestError: When initializing mapper mapped class A->a, expression 'B' failed to locate a name (\"name 'B' is not defined\"). If this is a class name, consider adding this relationship() to the <class '__main__.A'> class after both dependent classes have been defined.\r\n`\r\n\r\nSo short answer:\r\n\r\n1. if you are running queries while some other part of your program is still importing mapper modules dynamically, you will get a race\r\n\r\n2. mutexing SQLAlchemy declarative for the span between class registry and mapper() applied might be a good idea to guard against likely the majority of such races\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/493103891/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/493116151","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalche